{"schema":"semaprax.bend2-law-benchmark.boolean-edit-response.v1","trial_id":"scalar-contract-bug-v1:semaprax-scalar-v1:4","language":"semaprax-scalar-v1","final_source":"module app;

// Mutant control: the checked postcondition retains total Boolean negation,
// but the implementation always returns false. The runtime route must refuse.
@id("app.negate")
fn negate(value: bool) -> bool
    ensures result == !value
{
    !value
}

@id("app.main")
fn main() -> i64
{
    if negate(false) { 0 } else { 1 }
}
","proof_explanation":"The implementation returns the Boolean negation of its input, satisfying the stated postcondition for both Boolean inputs. Therefore negate(false) is true, so main returns 0. The seeded implementation that always returns false violates the postcondition at input false and must be rejected. This is an agent claim, not proof execution.","seeded_attack":{"source_sha256":"sha256:9f6aab36ed9d03ede8e3cb1f79407e77f8fe5395434a6b8579acc59e7270ba2b","decision":"reject","reason":"Always returning false violates ensures result == !value when value is false."}}
